@startuml
'=============================================================================
' KIND      INTENDED -- the product-level journey as the authority
'           documents describe it. It is NOT a function-by-function call
'           trace; for the measured structure see
'           05-package-dependencies.puml, and for the data path of
'           established operation see 08-operational-data-flow.puml.
' GROUNDING README.md ("Current product direction", "What is implemented
'           now"); PRODUCT.md ("The intended journey" steps 1-6).
'=============================================================================
!theme plain
title Learning Lab — intended product journey (high-level sequence)

actor Operator
participant "Company data" as Data
participant "adapters" as Adapters
participant "inspector" as Inspector
participant "modeller" as Modeller
participant "taskmodel + task family" as Model
participant "worker" as Worker
participant "fleet / system map" as Fleet
participant "supervisor" as Supervisor

Operator -> Data : provide incoming operational data
Data -> Adapters : read permitted input
Adapters -> Inspector : normalized structural representation
Inspector -> Inspector : measure observable facts
Inspector -> Modeller : evidence / observed structure
Operator -> Modeller : describe purpose / answer load-bearing questions
Modeller -> Model : propose explicit task model
Model --> Modeller : validation / task semantics
Modeller --> Operator : deterministic preview + required confirmations
Operator -> Modeller : establish/confirm where required
Modeller -> Worker : establish versioned deterministic work

loop recurring operation
  Data -> Worker : production input
  Worker -> Model : execute explicit task semantics
  Model --> Worker : result / refusal
  Worker -> Fleet : run provenance / effects / exception state
end

Operator -> Fleet : inspect company flow and current state
Fleet -> Supervisor : read-only company/fleet context
Operator -> Supervisor : ask / investigate
Supervisor --> Operator : interpretation grounded in referents/evidence
Supervisor ..> Fleet : proposed investigation/improvement only

note over Operator,Supervisor
This is the product-level journey described by README.md / PRODUCT.md.
It is not a function-by-function call trace.
end note
@enduml
